plit averages 2.5. Since the two copies run the same policy and the role is unknown, cooperating on every observation comes out best at an expected 2.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying P-FDT to two copies of the same model reading the same essay, each with different observations like names and leads. I'm treating the policy as a map from observations to actions, and asking what utility each copy gets. For Rowan, that's the negative of the sentence length, given both its own action and Sasha's.\n\nUnder the ex ante view, before anyone knows which role they hold, I'm weighing the payoffs: both quiet gives 2 years each, both defect gives 4, and the mixed split averages 2.5. Since the two copies run the same policy and the role is unknown, cooperating on every observation comes out best at an expected 2.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10047,"completion_tokens":909,"total_tokens":10956,"cost":0.058368,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.058368,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040188,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01818},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":499,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}